\newlabel{fig:geometry-gradients}{{1}{38}{Computational work to a common stationarity tolerance. The full original-coordinate KKT residual plus its tracked numerical budget is plotted against cumulative gradient evaluations for S3, S4, and S6 in panels (a), (b), and (c). FA is solid and UA is dashed. Both methods use non-restarted FISTA, $h=0.2$, $\lambda =0.01$, and their respective $\lambda =0.025$ starts. The horizontal line is $10^{-7}$. Curves end at their FISTA stopping points, before the local refinement in Section~\ref {subsec:polish-results}}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{subsec:polish-results}{{6.3}{39}{Active-face refinement resolves late-stage residuals}{subsection.6.3}{}}
\newlabel{tab:polish-results}{{3}{39}{Full original-coordinate KKT residuals for one-step refinement of the UA fits}{table.3}{}}
\newlabel{subsec:cv-results}{{6.4}{39}{Training selection and factor-mediated prediction}{subsection.6.4}{}}
\newlabel{tab:cv-selection}{{4}{40}{Training-only penalty selections and full-training refit residuals. A star denotes the upper grid boundary}{table.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:cv-paths-local}{{2}{41}{Training-only three-fold validation paths on S1--S6 in panels (a)--(f). FA uses solid lines and circles; UA uses dashed lines and triangles. Each score is the aggregate within-fold Gehan loss contrast against zero prediction; lower values are preferred. Diamonds mark selected penalties and asterisks mark the upper boundary of the original fixed grid. The S4 UA candidate at $\lambda =0.01$ has no aggregate score because one fold failed its numerical eligibility rule. Each panel uses one three-fold partition and its own vertical scale}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{tab:cv-model-summary}{{5}{42}{Selected full-training models. $\|\hat {\bm {\beta }}\|_0$ counts exact nonzero penalized coefficients; $\|\hat {\bm {b}}_{\rm pred}\|_0$ counts exact nonzero frozen prediction slopes. CV is the three-fold score at the selected penalty; smaller is better. FISTA and Newton columns count accepted updates in the full-training refit}{table.5}{}}
